Changed test assumptions: the old integer-census test required settlement while admission sampled without serialization; it now finishes admission before settlement and still proves stale censuses keep the budget charged. The new exact race tests independently cover concurrent settlement. Five existing record-reference/alias cases assumed immediate GC after removing a record selection; each now asserts retention refusal and explicitly ages the new clock before checking deletion and late-reference rejection. The excluded-entry reader test now asserts reader admission before/after collection, while re-enabling the tombstoned requirement is still refused.

